    "abstract": "The Segment Anything project introduces a new task, model and dataset for image segmentation. Using an efficient model in a data collection loop, the authors built the largest segmentation dataset to date, with over 1 billion masks on 11M licensed and privacy-respecting images. The promptable model transfers zero-shot to new image distributions and tasks, with zero-shot performance that is often competitive with or better than prior fully supervised results.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "A promptable segmentation task (return a valid mask for any point, box, mask or text prompt) enables zero-shot transfer via prompt engineering.",
      "SAM decouples a heavy image encoder (run once per image) from a lightweight prompt encoder and mask decoder that run in about 50 ms in a web browser.",
      "Predicting three masks per ambiguous prompt and back-propagating only the lowest-loss mask handles ambiguity.",
      "The data engine produced SA-1B: 1.1B masks on 11M images, 99.1% generated fully automatically."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
